  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0192, and it is used to store information about a company's departments, employees, projects, and project participation records. The schema consists of four tables: department, employee, project, and project_participation_record.\nThe department table contains information about the company's departments, including the department head, department ID, department name, and foreign key to the employee table. The employee table contains information about the employees, including their date of birth, department ID, employee number, gender, name, phone number, position, and foreign key to the department table.\nThe project table contains information about the company's projects, including the actual completion date, actual cost, estimated completion date, project budget, project location, project manager ID, project name, project number, project progress, start date, and foreign key to the employee table.\nThe project_participation_record table contains information about the participation of employees in projects, including the employee number, participation time, project number, role, work hours, and foreign keys to the employee and project tables. The primary key of this table is a composite key consisting of employee number, project number, and participation time.\nIn summary, the rschema_0192 database schema is used to store information about a company's departments, employees, projects, and project participation records. The schema consists of four tables, each with its own set of columns and foreign keys, which are used to enforce domain integrity, entity integrity, and referential integrity.",
  "gold_question": "The construction company undertakes multiple construction projects. Each project has a project manager, project name, start date, estimated completion date, actual completion date, project budget, and project location. The company has multiple departments, each responsible for different projects. Each department has a department name and department head. Each project involves multiple employees, and each employee can participate in multiple projects. Each employee has an employee number, name, date of birth, gender, phone number, and position. When an employee participates in a project, the project they participate in, participation time, role, and work hours need to be recorded. The project management information system needs to be able to track project progress and cost, as well as generate statistics on employee workload.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0192.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0192\nCREATE TABLE `department` (\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `department_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `department_head_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`department_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `department_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`department_head_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee` (\n  `employee_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `date_of_birth` date NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_number`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `department` (`department_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `project` (\n  `project_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `project_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `project_manager_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `start_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `estimated_completion_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `actual_completion_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `project_budget` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `actual_cost` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `project_location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `project_progress` int(3) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`project_number`),\n  CONSTRAINT `project_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`project_manager_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `project_participation_record` (\n  `employee_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `project_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `participation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `work_hours` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_number`, `project_number`, `participation_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `project_participation_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_number`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `project_participation_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`project_number`) REFERENCES `project` (`project_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
